      "rev_n_1_326051_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_326051_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_326051",
        "thought_text": "The current approach is incorrect because it doesn't properly handle the restrictions. The dynamic programming solution needs to be modified to account for the black edges along the paths specified by the restrictions. The current implementation only considers the coloring of individual subtrees, which doesn't capture the global constraint of having at least one black edge along the restricted paths.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_326051_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_786b3d362c",
        "created_at": 1794530339.6899545
      },
      "rev_n_2_0f3a00_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_0f3a00_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_0f3a00",
        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. The error in the previous implementation was in the interpretation of the problem. The code was correctly generating all possible edge paintings, but it wasn't properly handling the case where multiple restrictions could be satisfied by the same painting. The solution should count the number of paintings that satisfy all restrictions, not the number of paintings that satisfy each restriction individually. This requires a different approach to the problem.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_0f3a00_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_a1f7260df8",
        "created_at": 1794530418.2737515
      },
      "rev_n_3_e3f6ee_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_e3f6ee_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_e3f6ee",
        "thought_text": "I apologize for the oversight. The error in the previous implementation was in the backtracking function. The function was not correctly exploring all possible colorings. Let's refine the approach by using a more efficient bitmask-based solution that directly counts the valid colorings without explicitly generating all possibilities.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_e3f6ee_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_1549f2f5ec",
        "created_at": 1794530495.1958168
      },
      "rev_n_4_ed7bf7_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_ed7bf7_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_ed7bf7",
        "thought_text": "Revisit the dynamic programming approach by considering the restrictions more carefully. Instead of focusing on individual subtrees, consider how the restrictions affect the overall structure of valid colorings.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "3492573728461299810",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794530542.1699955
      },
      "rev_n_5_394d95_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_394d95_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_394d95",
        "thought_text": "Implement a bottom-up dynamic programming solution that starts from the leaves of the tree and works its way up. This approach can potentially handle the restrictions more efficiently by considering the impact of each restriction on the entire subtree.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "3492573728461299810",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794530542.1700199
      },
      "rev_n_6_f122f0_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_6_f122f0_0",
        "node_id": "n_6_f122f0",
        "thought_text": "Consider using a bitmask representation for the colorings of edges along each path. This can allow for more efficient storage and manipulation of the coloring states, potentially simplifying the handling of restrictions.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "3492573728461299810",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794530542.1700344
      },
      "rev_n_4_ed7bf7_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_ed7bf7_1",
        "node_id": "n_4_ed7bf7",
        "thought_text": "Instead of focusing on individual subtrees, consider how the restrictions affect the overall structure of valid colorings. The key insight is that we need to count the number of valid colorings that satisfy all restrictions simultaneously, rather than trying to adjust for restrictions after the fact. This approach ensures that we capture the global constraint of having at least one black edge along the restricted paths.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "3492573728461299810",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_4_ed7bf7_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_ea4c817c45",
        "created_at": 1794530583.3416498
      },
      "rev_n_5_394d95_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_394d95_1",
        "node_id": "n_5_394d95",
        "thought_text": "The current approach needs to be modified to correctly handle the restrictions. Instead of only considering the coloring of individual subtrees, we should propagate the information about black edges along the paths specified by the restrictions. This requires a more sophisticated dynamic programming solution that takes into account the global structure of the tree and the specific restrictions.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "3492573728461299810",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_5_394d95_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_0a1cfdfa14",
